From 42a94ceaf304337e354f50de11ab6c7c61d4cce5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hussain-maker <79055482+Hussain-maker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:21:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Target/focus: make the restricted-aura (combat) layout match
 X-Perl's

While aura data is secret (arena, rated PvP, M+, raid combat) the target and
focus frames show auras through Blizzard's AuraContainer, which ignored most
of X-Perl's aura settings. Now:

- The aura filter options apply, with the same rules as the normal layout:
  castable buffs, "only my buffs" on friends, "only my debuffs" on enemies,
  curable debuffs on friends.
- "Buff Countdown" shows an X-Perl-style countdown (yellow, whole seconds)
  drawn by the game via a duration text binding, hidden above the
  "Countdown Start" time by a step colour curve. Falls back to Blizzard's
  countdown numbers styled like X-Perl's if the API is unavailable.
- "Wrap Buffs" wraps at the frame's full width like the normal layout, and
  "Target Buff Rows" caps the number of icons.
- Debuffs get X-Perl's debuff border, coloured by dispel type by the game.
- New option "Key Enemy Buffs" (off by default): on enemies, show only
  important buffs, then purgeable ones.

Core: XPerl_AuraContainer_AddGroup (one group with X-Perl's button setup;
used by XPerl_AuraContainer_Create, which gains an optional maxCount). The
buff blacklist module now handles every buff group of a container.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
